> 
> if (is_human(ptr)) adjalign(-sgn(u.ualign.type));
>   if (is_demon(ptr)) adjalign(sgn(u.ualign.type));

That's just an alignment adjustment. (It's also a slightly peculiar one,
for various reasons that I've asked the DevTeam about.)

>   if(!(ptr->geno & G_GENO)) {
>    if(flags.soundok) {
>  /* fixme: unconditional "caverns" will be silly in some circumstances */
>        if(flags.verbose)
>    pline("A thunderous voice booms through the caverns:");
>        verbalize("No, mortal!  That will not be done.");
>    }
>    continue;

This isn't dependent on your being human, or (directly) on the target
being a demon; some monsters are marked as genocidable, some aren't.
As it happens, no demons are marked genocidable. (Which means that one
of the alignment adjustments above will currently never be applied.)

